# Talent Digger Project Conventions

## Tech Stack

- **Framework**: uni-app (WeChat mini-program target) + Vue 3 Composition API + TypeScript
- **Build**: Vite 5 with `@dcloudio/vite-plugin-uni`, dev via `UNI_PLATFORM=mp-weixin vite build --watch`
- **Testing**: vitest (unit tests for composables and utilities), 51 tests across 4 test files
- **Styles**: SCSS with common variables from `@/styles/common.scss` (via `@use`)
- **Package manager**: pnpm with workspace (`pnpm-workspace.yaml`)
- **Monorepo**: `miniapp/`, `shared/` (types), `admin/`

## Directory Structure

```
miniapp/src/
├── pages/          # uni-app pages (Vue SFC with <script setup lang="ts">)
├── composables/    # Vue composables (useAnswerLogic, usePlanLogic)
├── utils/          # Pure utilities (scoring, summary, error, navigate, devLogger)
├── api/            # CloudBase cloud function wrappers with mock fallbacks
├── data/mock/      # Mock questions, reports, test definitions
├── stores/         # Pinia stores (user)
├── styles/         # SCSS variables and common classes (common.scss)
├── __tests__/      # vitest unit tests (composable and utility tests only)
└── config.ts       # App config from import.meta.env.VITE_*
shared/types/       # Shared TypeScript interfaces (test.ts)
```

## Key Patterns

### Storage
- Use `uni.getStorageSync(key)` / `uni.setStorageSync(key, value)` for local persistence
- Key naming: `completedTests`, `lastAnswers`, `lastTestId`, `seenStageSummary`, `growthPlans`
- Always use `try/catch` around storage reads and provide defaults (e.g., `|| '[]'`)

### API
- Cloud functions called via `wx.cloud.callFunction({ name, data })` with 8s timeout
- Every API function has a mock/local fallback when cloud is unavailable
- API response type: `{ code: number, message: string, data: T }` (`code === 0` = success)

### Pages (Vue SFC)
- Use `<script setup lang="ts">` exclusively
- Import from `@dcloudio/uni-app`: `onLoad`, `onShow`, `ref`, `computed`
- Import from `@/utils`: `smartNavigate` (handles tabbar vs regular navigation)
- SCSS: `@use '@/styles/common.scss' as *;` at top of `<style lang="scss" scoped>`
- Use `$primary-color`, `$text-primary`, `$text-secondary`, `$text-hint`, `$shadow`, etc.

### Composables
- Export a factory function (e.g., `useAnswerLogic()`) returning reactive state + methods
- Use `ref` + `toRaw` + spread for answer reactivity (avoid Proxy set-trap in WeChat runtime)
- Test every composable with vitest — test reactivity, accumulation, boundary cases

### Scoring
- Talent compass: 26 questions × 4 options, each option maps to 10 dimensions (logic, creativity, memory, observation, comm, lead, exec, empathy, resilience, learn)
- `computeDimensionScores(answers, questions, { normalize: true })` returns `{ dimKey: percentage }`
- `topDimensions(scores, 3)` returns top-3 dimension keys sorted by score

## Nav System

```typescript
// TabBar pages (use switchTab)
const TAB_BAR_PAGES = [
  '/pages/index/index',
  '/pages/test/index',
  '/pages/career/index',
  '/pages/plan/index',
  '/pages/mine/index',
]
// All other pages use navigateTo
smartNavigate('/pages/test/answer?testId=xxx')
```

## Dev Workflow

- `pnpm dev` (in miniapp/) = `UNI_PLATFORM=mp-weixin vite build --watch`
- `pnpm test` = `vitest run`
- `pnpm log:server` = `node scripts/weapp-log-server.cjs` (dev error logging bridge)
- Dev errors auto-posted to `http://127.0.0.1:8787/log` in WeChat devtools

## Test Conventions

- Test files: `src/__tests__/<name>.test.ts`, import from `@/` alias
- Use `vitest` (describe/it/expect) with `jsdom` environment
- Test composables in isolation (no uni-app runtime needed)
- Focus on: reactivity accumulation, boundary conditions, normalization, computed outputs
- Run: `cd miniapp && npx vitest run`
